      <profileDesc>
         <abstract>
            <ab>According to this gadl, the spiritual father of 
               <persName ref="PRS3801endreyas"><roleName type="title">ʾAbuna</roleName> ʾƎndrǝyās</persName>  was 
               <persName ref="PRS4282GabraKr">Gabra Krǝstos of Dabra Salodā</persName>. <persName ref="PRS3801endreyas"/>
               was an itinerant monk, who spent the greater part of his life in <placeName ref="LOC1945Bogos"/>, where he encountered 
               pilgrims traveling to <placeName ref="LOC3957Jerusa"/>. One of these pilgrims was <persName ref="PRS9059Taamna"/>,
               who was to remain with him. The commemoration of <persName ref="PRS3801endreyas"/> falls on 
               <date ref="ethiocal:Yakkatit1">the first of Yakkātit</date>. The gadl was composed at the behest of the Holy Spirit, as conveyed 
               by Melchisedek to the monk <persName ref="PRS4358Gabrase">Gabra Śəllase</persName>, who asked another monk, 
               <persName ref="PRS8322saggaHa">Ṣaggā Hāymanot</persName>, to write it down.</ab>
         </abstract>
